@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# v40 — MuMu mouse control and compact Loong Lens UI
+
+This build returns to the v37 codebase and removes the v38/v39 ADB capture/input
+changes. It uses desktop screenshots and guarded Windows mouse control for
+MuMuPlayer 6.8.9, Android 15, portrait 1080×1920 at 480 DPI, as supplied.
+
+MuMu's running game tab can be named Android Device or after the game. Window
+selection uses its process identity and portrait dimensions rather than requiring
+a BlueStacks title. The device manager, browser/document windows and unsupported
+landscape layouts are excluded. Native child-window bounds identify the Android
+viewport; when unavailable, its 9:16 portrait area is fitted below the top toolbar
+using native client edges. One transform drives capture, clicks, held drags and
+Map Tweaker markers. The toolbar receives no game clicks or dots; native resize pixels never receive
+mouse input. Capture retains the complete render child even when the resize
+hit band overlaps it; mouse clipping is calculated independently.
+A window move, resize, changed render child, loss of focus, cover or F10 releases
+mouse input and stops the current operation. No ADB executable or Android helper
+is included or called.
+
+Loong Lens defaults to 1000×760 rather than 1440×940, with a 960×720 minimum.
+Sidebar, text, card spacing, buttons and preview are compact. Start, Stop/F10,
+Reset, the daily counter, Obtained, Endless and settings stay accessible. The
+main window opens beside a visible MuMu window when the desktop has room.
+
+Exit the older Loong Lens completely, extract the whole folder and run the new
+LoongLens.exe (header v40). Start the MuMu Android device and launch the game;
+keep the portrait window with its toolbar at the top, visible/uncovered/focused.
+Use the game's default map zoom. Configure map-button positions in Sniper
+Settings if your saved calibration differs. The settings picker shows the same
+normalized game image used for route recognition and input.
+
+Existing routes, all histories/screenshots, game-day counter/reset, Obtained
+choices, Endless, 20-second collection/return, F10, route exclusions, four map
+control boxes and heatmap stay on the v37 behavior. No changes to world data,
+recognition atlas or detector assets. Existing LocalAppData data is retained.
+
+Validation includes all prior tests, pure geometry/window-identity regressions,
+source/frozen layout checks at 960×720, 1000×760 and 1120×800, plus actual Windows
+capture/mouse/hotkeys on a disposable MuMu-shaped window. The independent test
+uses the supplied 560×1033 frame, 40-pixel toolbar and 558×992 game surface, verifies
+atlas alignment and actual delivered click coordinates, held motion and F10.
+It does not run a live MuMu/Android game or establish real route speed. A full
+76-view atlas comparison with v37 and archive SHA256 verification are included.
+
